\section*{Rigidity of Completely Close \$C\textasciicircum{}*\$-Algebras}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For any prescribed small unitary displacement, the paper claims one uniform Kadison--Kastler tolerance guaranteeing conjugacy of close unital von Neumann algebras on any complex Hilbert space. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For every $\varepsilon>0$, OpenAI claims a single $\delta(\varepsilon)>0$ valid for every complex Hilbert space $H$ and all unital von Neumann algebras $M,N\subset B(H)$ with common identity: if their norm-unit-ball Hausdorff distance $d(M,N)<\delta$, then
\[
\exists u\in B(H):\quad u^*u=uu^*=I_H,\quad uMu^*=N,\quad\|u-I_H\|<\varepsilon.
\]
No separability, type or injectivity hypothesis is imposed on these von Neumann algebras.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 289, 2026-09-23): For finite factors, free-word estimates control amplification while boundary averaging corrects nearby unitaries into a measurable cocycle. Double ergodicity makes the resulting correspondence multiplicative and yields a spatial implementation. Properly infinite algebras are handled through matrix amplification and modular preparation; alignment of centers and limits over separable restrictions assemble the universal conclusion.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 289, 2026-09-23): The primary manuscript establishes uniform near-identity unitary conjugacy of sufficiently two-sided close unital von Neumann algebras. The theorem gives spatial isomorphism and near-identity conjugacy for the von Neumann, common-identity subcase. This problem also quantifies over general C*-algebras and asks about their structural invariants at completely bounded distance; that full class is not covered.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 289, the scope page documents the following selections. The selection gives a tolerance depending only on the requested distance of an implementing unitary from identity, for two close common-identity von Neumann algebras. The separate one-way near-inclusion and general norm-closed examples are outside it. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Comparator files: StrongKadisonKastler.lean. Declarations: OAI.KadisonKastler.universal\_strong\_stability.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{Universal strong Kadison–Kastler stability}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:Universal-strong-Kadison-Kastler-stability-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Universal-strong-Kadison-Kastler-stability-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Universal-strong-Kadison-Kastler-stability-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Universal-strong-Kadison-Kastler-stability-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/Universal-strong-Kadison-Kastler-stability-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Universal-strong-Kadison-Kastler-stability-September-23-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex\#L18}{thm:main}.
\item Family 289: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/289.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/StrongKadisonKastler.json}{Comparator StrongKadisonKastler.json}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/StrongKadisonKastler.lean}{Comparator StrongKadisonKastler.lean}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
